1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,770
In 2009, young scientists

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,550
investigated fifteen detox products.

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:08,240
Two questions for their makers.

4
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:09,370
What does detox mean?

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,850
And where's the proof?

6
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,870
No two companies

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,490
defined it the same way.

8
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,090
Most offered no evidence.

9
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,820
Oh, and one product?

10
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,200
A hair straightener.

11
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:20,200
So before buying a cleanse,

12
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:21,640
ask what it's actually

13
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:23,130
meant to remove.

14
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,120
Detox diets lack convincing evidence

15
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,260
for removing toxins.

16
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:28,680
Your liver processes harmful substances;

17
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:30,300
your kidneys filter waste.

18
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,640
No straightener required.
